4. Audio — Qari Recitation
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Status:       PERMITTED USE, NOT A FREE LICENSE (D3, reviewed 2026-08-15).
              Served from the Al Quran Cloud / Islamic Network CDN, which
              states the recitations are licensed to them by the reciters
              or their estates. Copyright remains with the reciters and
              removal may be requested, so this is documented permission
              with a takedown clause rather than a closed decision.
Qari:         Mahmoud Khalil Al-Husary, murattal (edition ar.husary)
Host:         Al Quran Cloud / Islamic Network
URL:          https://cdn.islamic.network/quran/audio/128/ar.husary/{n}.mp3
              ({n} = mushaf position 1..6236)
Terms:        https://alquran.cloud/terms-and-conditions (section IV)
              "Recitations are licensed to us by the reciters or their
              estates for free, non-commercial redistribution at the
              bitrates we publish. You may stream, embed and download them
              for personal and educational use. You may bundle them into a
              commercial product, but please note that copyrights lie with
              the reciters and they may ask you to remove the conent."
Retrieved:    2026-08-15
Conditions:   Do not re-encode or rehost — the grant is scoped to the
              bitrates the CDN publishes. Attribute the reciter.

Underlying rights: the Quran text is public domain, but a recording carries
separate performer and producer rights. Al-Husary died 1980-11-24; Egyptian
terms likely lapsed, but EU (70 yrs) and US (URAA/MMA) terms may still run.
Not treated as public domain. Not legal advice.

Previously EveryAyah.com — removed 2026-08-15. It publishes no license for
the audio at all; its only licensing text covers the separate timing files
and points at a URL that 404s. The "EveryAyah is CC-BY-NC" claim in
circulation originates from a third party requesting clarification
(quran/quran_android#434), not from any rights holder.

Rejected alternatives: Wikimedia Commons (verified licenses, but no complete
per-ayah mushaf); QUL/Tarteel (licensing varies per resource, none stated for
the Al-Husary set); Archive.org mirrors (uploader-asserted status only).

See docs/audio-sources.md for the full review.

